---How a view updates its materialized table in place rather than rebuilding it.
---@class posthog.warehouse_saved_queries.IncrementalConfig
---@field enabled? boolean Whether runs update the table incrementally instead of rebuilding it.
---@field incremental_key string Output column whose advancing value marks rows as new. Each run reads only rows at or after the last run's highest value for it. When the query groups, this must be one of the grouped columns, so every group a run touches is recomputed in full.
---@field unique_key posthog.warehouse_saved_queries.IncrementalConfigUniqueKeyList Output columns that identify a row, used to match recomputed rows against stored ones. Must include every GROUP BY column. These columns can never be null.
---@field lookback_seconds? number How far back before the last run's high point to re-read, so late-arriving data is picked up. Only applies when the incremental key is a date or time.

---Output columns that identify a row, used to match recomputed rows against stored ones. Must include every GROUP BY column. These columns can never be null.
---@alias posthog.warehouse_saved_queries.IncrementalConfigUniqueKeyList string[]

---Whether a query can be materialized incrementally, and what stands in the way.
---@class posthog.warehouse_saved_queries.IncrementalEligibility
---@field eligible boolean True when nothing blocks incremental materialization.
---@field key_candidates posthog.warehouse_saved_queries.IncrementalEligibilityKeyCandidatesList Output columns that could be used as the incremental key. Excludes aggregates, columns whose type cannot serve as an advancing watermark (strings, booleans, arrays), and for a union only includes columns every branch produces.
---@field unique_key_candidates posthog.warehouse_saved_queries.IncrementalEligibilityUniqueKeyCandidatesList Output columns the unique key may be built from. A superset of key_candidates: identifying a row only needs equality, so strings qualify here even though they cannot be the incremental key.
---@field key_candidate_types posthog.warehouse_saved_queries.IncrementalEligibilityKeyCandidateTypesMap Coarse type per candidate, keyed by column name: datetime, date, integer, decimal, float, string, or uuid. A candidate with no entry has a type the check could not determine.
---@field blockers posthog.warehouse_saved_queries.IncrementalEligibilityBlockersList Reasons this query cannot be incremental. Each names the construct responsible.
---@field warnings posthog.warehouse_saved_queries.IncrementalEligibilityWarningsList Things that still work but are worth knowing, such as a filter that cannot be pushed down so each run reads as much data as a full refresh.

